    "level": "ordinary",
    "year": null,
    "question": "$f(x) = \\frac{x^2 - 9}{x - 3}$, where $x \\neq 3$.\nBy investigating the values of $f(x)$ for $x$ close to $3$, find the limiting value of $f(x)$ as $x \\to 3$.",
    "marks": 10,
    "steps": [
     {
      "title": "Simplify the function for $x \\neq 3$",
      "lines": [
       {
        "tex": "\\frac{x^2 - 9}{x - 3} &= \\frac{(x-3)(x+3)}{x-3}"
       },
       {
        "tex": "&= x + 3"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "title": "Try values just below and just above 3",
      "lines": [
       {
        "tex": "f(2.99) &= 2.99 + 3 = 5.99"
       },
       {
        "tex": "f(3.01) &= 3.01 + 3 = 6.01"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "title": "State the limiting value",
      "lines": [
       {
        "text": "From both sides, $f(x)$ gets closer and closer to $6$."
       },
       {
        "tex": "\\lim_{x \\to 3} f(x) &= 3 + 3 = 6"
       }
      ]
     }
    ],
    "final": "6"
